A||N||5||MIKLAV||'86 V-6  W/AUTO Looking for grounding strap Location||||1||
Z||000000||MIKLAV||10-15-2000||03:22 PM||||I am puzzled. I have an '86 V-6 Auto.  I R&R the engine from the car and cradle but for the life of me I can't remember where a black copper insulatade stran wire goes. The one end of the wire I nevered removed.  The nevered removed end is connected directly to a stud which in turns goes to the engine block.  The stud is located lower drivers side of the engine in between the firewall and engine block. The wire is about 14 inches long.  I don't know where the other end grounds to.  I painted the cradle so if it did ground to the cradle I can't see it.  Any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||10-15-2000||06:20 PM||||I was just going over ground straps on my 88 auto. I'm trying to remember that one, but I'm coming up fuzzy. I remeber 1 that was for the deck lid on the driver side, but I don't think that one went to the engine. I remeber the big black cable that goest from the battery to the engine mount I beleive, and I remeber the one that goes from the top A/C bracket to some frame point by the battery... or I could just be missing one. my parts were a little scattered when I got back to the shop (damn public shops!!)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-15-2000||06:35 PM||||If I am thinking of the same one you are, I think it goes to the bottem bolt on the passenger side rear decklid mounting location. Its the one on the car, not the lid itself. The one I am thinking of is a bare flat copper wire. Hope this helps. P.S. Mine is an 86GT 2.8.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000003||MIKLAV||10-15-2000||10:54 PM||||Thanks for the reply, but one I am tring to figure out is on the other side and down near the engine cradle.<BR>Mike<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>If I am thinking of the same one you are, I think it goes to the bottem bolt on the passenger side rear decklid mounting location. Its the one on the car, not the lid itself. The one I am thinking of is a bare flat copper wire. Hope this helps. P.S. Mine is an 86GT 2.8.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||10-15-2000||11:05 PM||||Look for a stud on the driver's side fenderwell inside the engine bay down low kind of below where the A/C hoses are routed along the left wall of the engine bay.<P>It's a bit of a pain to reach either from the top or the bottom.  It is basically a self tapping screw on one end (the one threaded into the fender well) and a machine thread stud on the other end with I believe a 10mm nut.<P>I believe it will actually be easier to reach from the top.  When I loosened mine to replace the wire the stud unthreaded from the fenderwell.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000005||MIKLAV||10-16-2000||12:00 PM||||Thank you Caroll.<BR>Mike<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Carrolles:<BR><B>Look for a stud on the driver's side fenderwell inside the engine bay down low kind of below where the A/C hoses are routed along the left wall of the engine bay.<P>It's a bit of a pain to reach either from the top or the bottom.  It is basically a self tapping screw on one end (the one threaded into the fender well) and a machine thread stud on the other end with I believe a 10mm nut.<P>I believe it will actually be easier to reach from the top.  When I loosened mine to replace the wire the stud unthreaded from the fenderwell.<P>Hope this helps,<P>Carroll</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
